      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can use the magnitude of the cross product of these vectors. The cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\) will give a vector whose magnitude is the area of the parallelogram.\n\nThe cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\) is calculated as follows:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 4 \\end{vmatrix} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1) = -2\\mathbf{i} - 14\\mathbf{j} - 10\\mathbf{k} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of this vector is:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
